ocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:147:## ADR-018 — Old goal-selection artifacts are not current codebase truth\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:155:## ADR-019 — The pipeline must advance the game while it is being built\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:163:## ADR-020 — Style evaluation is an evaluator specialization, not a separate architecture\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:173:## ADR-021 — Task decomposition is progressive and just-in-time\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:181:## ADR-022 — Missing design creates an artifact proposal, not silent invention\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:189:## ADR-023 — Generated design requires authority before generation\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:197:## ADR-024 — Approved artifacts may become subordinate project design state\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:207:## ADR-025 — Reconciliation results are immutable point-in-time snapshots\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:217:## ADR-026 — Reconciliation proposes graph deltas but never directly mutates the persistent graph\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:229:## ADR-027 — Reconciliation bootstrap requires independent multi-model verification\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:242:## ADR-029 — Design decomposition and execution scope are separate axes\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:250:## ADR-030 — Current output view is mutable; run history stays nested and immutable\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:260:## ADR-035 — Provider-adapter enforcement\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:274:## ADR-036 — Own the narrow Claude Code and OpenAI/Codex transport adapters\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:288:## ADR-039 — Separate generic invocation from NSC task execution\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/DECISIONS.md:298:## ADR-040 — OpenAI/Codex AgentRuntime and ArchitectureReview migration\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md:1:# No Safe Circle — Autonomous AI Development Pipeline\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md:3:## Master Context / Architecture Handoff\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md:11:## Cu