{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n --glob '\"'!Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/**'\"' --glob '\"'!Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/AgentRuntime/**'\"' 'Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype\\\\.unity|Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype\\\\.unity' Tasks Pipeline Docs Assets Assignment6GER AgentCrew DynamicContentPipeline GoalOrientedAgent | head -n 300\"","aggregated_output":"ilt) because the scene is only regenerated when a human runs the 'No Safe Circle/Build Door Prototype Scene' menu command in the Unity Editor, which has not happened in this container (consistent with implementation_result.json's remaining_work). This is expected given the project rule to use the scene-builder script rather than hand-editing scene YAML, not a contract violation, but the scene asset will not reflect the fix until a human re-runs the builder in Unity.\",\r\nAssignment6GER/outputs/evaluation_pass_1.json:41:    \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\r\nAgentCrew/outputs/validation_report.json:94:    \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\r\nAgentCrew/outputs/implementation_summary.md:219:Not created by this agent: `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`. Per the contract, this file must only be produced by running the menu command inside the Unity Editor and is intentionally not hand-authored.\r\nAgentCrew/outputs/implementation_summary.md:234:3. The command creates/replaces `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` containing: a floor plane, two flanking wall cubes forming a doorway gap, a door root (trigger zone + visual/blocking door cube), a player capsule with `CharacterController`, a directional light, a camera, a Canvas with an interaction prompt, a progress-fill image, a top-left Controls HUD panel, an `EventSystem` using `InputSystemUIInputModule`, and a labeled \"DEBUG: Take Damage (K)\" button.\r\nAgentCrew/outputs/feature_contract.json:50:      \"requirement\": \"The Editor menu command 'No Safe Circle/Build Door Prototype Scene' generates a complete, playable scene at Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity containing a floor, player placeholder, sealed door/doorway, camera, lighting, interaction UI, and a documented damage-test control, with all serialized references auto-wired.\",\r\nAgentCrew/outputs/feature_contract.json:144:      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md:391:- authoritative centralized scene: `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`;\nAgentCrew/outputs/run_report.md:51:- (Produced only by a human running the Editor menu command, not by this crew: `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`)\r\nTasks/NSC-026.yaml:20:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\r\nTasks/NSC-026.yaml:87:      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nTasks/NSC-025.yaml:21:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\r\nTasks/NSC-025.yaml:83:      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nDocs/AI-Pipeline/01_MILESTONE_TASK_GRAPH.md:321:- `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`\r\nAssets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs:16:        private const string CanonicalScenePath = \"Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\";\r\nTasks/NSC-023.yaml:75:      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nPipeline/TaskGraph/PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.yaml:173:      \"evidence\": \"Directly stated in Section 5 Current Prototype Scene Evidence; confirmed present via Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity and Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity glob results.\"\r\nPipeline/TaskGraph/PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.yaml:182:          \"requirement\": \"Scene-authoring work that changes objects generated or maintained through Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs must take exclusive-write locks on both that builder and Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity.\"\r\nAssets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/CommittedSceneCameraConformanceTests.cs:13:        private const string CanonicalScenePath = \"Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\";\r\nPipeline/TaskGraph/RESOURCE_GROUPS.yaml:108:      \"resource_key\": \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nTasks/NSC-021.yaml:23:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nTasks/NSC-005.yaml:83:      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nTasks/NSC-020.yaml:19:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\r\nTasks/NSC-004.yaml:18:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\r\nTasks/NSC-004.yaml:86:      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nPipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/NSC-023/records/BASE-NSC-023-86af98f41ab5.json:31:      \"path\": \"Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nPipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/NSC-023/records/BASE-NSC-023-86af98f41ab5.json:36:      \"path\": \"Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity.meta\",\r\nPipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/NSC-023/records/BASE-NSC-023-86af98f41ab5.json:75:      \"notes\": \"Clean EditMode validation passed the in-memory builder camera checks and direct inspection of the authoritative Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity fixed orthographic isometric camera.\"\r\nPipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/NSC-023/records/BASE-NSC-023-86af98f41ab5.json:97:    \"notes\": \"The human approver explicitly opened Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity without rebuilding it, entered Play Mode, and confirmed orthographic isometric presentation, player-follow translation, fixed camera rotation, usable initial framing, and no blocking missing-reference or Console errors. Git remained clean after the check.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-009.yaml:20:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nTasks/NSC-019.yaml:22:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\r\nTasks/NSC-019.yaml:134:      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nTasks/NSC-003.yaml:19:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\r\nTasks/NSC-003.yaml:102:      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nTasks/NSC-008.yaml:21:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nTasks/NSC-007.yaml:21:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nPipeline/GDDRAG/knowledge_base/No_Safe_Circle_GDD_RAG.json:725:      \"text\": \"- **Minimal-context dispatch is a required pipeline constraint:** agents receive only the approved feature brief, its acceptance criteria, the relevant GDD rules, and the files plus scene/prefab information required for the active task. Unrelated project files or broad project context are not included unless the task genuinely requires them.\\n- Independent agents work in isolated branches or workspaces so their changes can be reviewed before integration.\\n- **Current prototype scene-builder lock:** scene-authoring work that changes objects generated or maintained through `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs` must take exclusive-write locks on both that builder and `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`. This specifically applies to doorway-crossing work that creates/configures the forward-side crossing trigger and, under the current scene-built UI approach, to final-victory work that creates/configures the **You Escaped** overlay. If a later approved architecture moves the overlay or another scene object into a separately owned runtime prefab/asset, the task may lock that actual asset instead; the task graph must reflect the implementation that exists when it is dispatched.\\n- Each task produces changed files, an implementation summary, known risks, and a Play Mode test checklist.\\n- Source control commits serve as the handoff between implementation, validation, and integration.\\n- Agents may report a risk or recommend a scope cut, but they cannot redesign the game or add features without developer approval.\\n- The human developer remains responsible for architecture, merging changes, inspecting Unity scenes and prefabs, playtesting, balance, and final integration.\",\r\nPipeline/GDDRAG/knowledge_base/No_Safe_Circle_GDD_RAG.json:816:      \"text\": \"As of the August 20, 2026 repository state, the project contains three committed `.unity` scene files. Reconciliation and planning must describe them accurately rather than treating every scene file as an equivalent gameplay scene:\\n\\n- `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` is the current canonical gameplay prototype scene and is the scene maintained by `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs`.\\n- `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` is a small non-canonical stub containing the default-style Main Camera and Directional Light; its camera is perspective, not the orthographic isometric gameplay camera. It must not be cited as an alternative implemented gameplay prototype.\\n- `Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity` is also a non-canonical stub/sample scene and must not be described as the only or primary gameplay scene.\\n- The presence of these stubs is repository evidence, not a design requirement. Their deletion, retention, or repurposing is a **human decision**; agents and reconciliation steps must not delete or reinterpret them merely to make scene inventory evidence cleaner.\",\r\nPipeline/GDDRAG/knowledge_base/No_Safe_Circle_GDD_RAG.json:963:      \"text\": \"- **Unity 2D Tilemap Editor** (`com.unity.2d.tilemap`) is approved and required for the intended Isometric Tilemap authoring workflow. If it is absent from `Packages/manifest.json`, adding/configuring it is concrete project-configuration work, not deferred design.\\n- **Unity AI Navigation** (`com.unity.ai.navigation`) is the approved enemy-navigation implementation. If it is absent from `Packages/manifest.json`, adding/configuring it is a prerequisite for the gameplay navigation/locomotion layer and locomotion-dependent enemy work.\\n- The required delivery target is a **Windows Standalone build**. The current canonical gameplay scene is `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`; that scene (or a later human-approved replacement canonical gameplay scene) must be registered in Unity Build Settings before the Windows delivery requirement can be considered complete. A committed `EditorBuildSettings.asset` with no registered canonical gameplay scene is confirmed incomplete build configuration and must remain represented as open configuration work. The top-level `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` and `Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity` stubs do not satisfy this requirement merely because they are `.unity` files.\\n- Package-manifest and ProjectSettings changes authorized by these approved requirements may be implemented by an agent, but the developer must inspect the resulting package state, scene registration, and Windows build configuration before merge.\",\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/prompts/reconcile.md:552:- `unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/prompts/reconcile.md:1739:unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/prompts/reconcile.md:1797:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/prompts/reconcile.md:1853:unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/prompts/reconcile.md:1875:unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/prompts/reconcile.md:1938:For the current repository architecture, `gameplay-navigation-locomotion` is expected to integrate the NavMesh/walkability representation into the canonical scene objects generated by `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs`. The current builder clears and recreates `Floor`, `Walls`, and `DoorRoot`, and saves `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`.\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/prompts/reconcile.md:1944:- `unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/outputs/current/PROPOSED_GRAPH_DELTA.md:18:| player-movement | implementation | Mouse-Directed Player Movement, Shared Pointer Projection, and Movement Restriction | open | single_agent | repo-file:Assets/InputSystem_Actions.inputactions, repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs, unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity | player |  |\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/outputs/current/PROPOSED_GRAPH_DELTA.md:19:| player-health | implementation | Player Health Ownership, Restore, Death Transition, and Feedback | open | single_agent | repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs, unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity | player |  |\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/outputs/current/PROPOSED_GRAPH_DELTA.md:22:| fireball | implementation | Charged Fireball | open | single_agent | repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs, unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity, repo-file:Assets/InputSystem_Actions.inputactions | combat | player-movement, enemy-health-damage-defeat |\r\nPipeline/Reconciliation/outputs/current/PROPOSED_GRAPH_DELTA.md:23:| f