{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py | sed -n '205,255p' && nl -ba Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '1,78p;629,687p' && nl -ba Pipeline/Testing/scene_location_smoke_test.py | sed -n '1,90p' && nl -ba Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md | sed -n '66,152p'\"","aggregated_output":"   205\t                    if not evidence[\"path\"].startswith(artifact_prefix):\r\n   206\t                        invalid.append(_finding(\"artifact_location_invalid\", f\"Gate artifact is outside {artifact_prefix}.\", record))\r\n   207\t                        artifact_bad = True\r\n   208\t                    elif not repo.exists(head, evidence[\"path\"]) or repo.blob(head, evidence[\"path\"]) != evidence[\"blob_sha\"]:\r\n   209\t                        invalid.append(_finding(\"artifact_blob_mismatch\", f\"Evidence artifact {evidence['path']} is absent or altered at HEAD.\", record))\r\n   210\t                        artifact_bad = True\r\n   211\t            if artifact_bad:\r\n   212\t                continue\r\n   213\t        except (ConformanceRecordError, json.JSONDecodeError, UnicodeDecodeError) as exc:\r\n   214\t            invalid.append(_finding(\"record_object_unavailable\", str(exc), record))\r\n   215\t            continue\r\n   216\t\r\n   217\t        if not repo.is_ancestor(state[\"commit\"], head):\r\n   218\t            stale.append(record)\r\n   219\t            continue\r\n   220\t\r\n   221\t        record_gate_ids = [gate[\"gate_id\"] for gate in data[\"gate_results\"]]\r\n   222\t        if record_gate_ids != current_gate_ids and set(record_gate_ids) != set(current_gate_ids):\r\n   223\t            invalid.append(_finding(\"completion_gate_set_mismatch\", \"Record does not contain exactly the current completion-gate set.\", record))\r\n   224\t            continue\r\n   225\t        contract_changed = contract[\"path\"] != task_path or contract[\"revision\"] != current_revision or contract[\"sha256\"] != current_contract_hash\r\n   226\t        if contract_changed:\r\n   227\t            replan.append(record)\r\n   228\t            continue\r\n   229\t        approval = data[\"human_approval\"]\r\n   230\t        if approval[\"required\"] and (approval[\"decision\"] != \"approved\" or not approval[\"approved_by\"].strip()):\r\n   231\t            human.append(record)\r\n   232\t            continue\r\n   233\t        if (not approval[\"required\"] and approval[\"decision\"] != \"not_required\"):\r\n   234\t            invalid.append(_finding(\"human_approval_contradictory\", \"Non-required approval must use not_required.\", record))\r\n   235\t            continue\r\n   236\t        if changed_surface or canon[\"path\"] != CANON_PATH or canon[\"sha256\"] != current_canon_hash:\r\n   237\t            stale.append(record)\r\n   238\t            continue\r\n   239\t        conformant.append(record)\r\n   240\t\r\n   241\t    if invalid:\r\n   242\t        return ConformanceState(task_id, title, \"invalid_evidence\", head, head_tree, None, tuple(invalid), dirty)\r\n   243\t    if conformant:\r\n   244\t        maximal = _maximal(repo, conformant)\r\n   245\t        if len(maximal) != 1:\r\n   246\t            ids = \", \".join(item.record_id for item in maximal)\r\n   247\t            return ConformanceState(task_id, title, \"ambiguous_evidence\", head, head_tree, None,\r\n   248\t                (_finding(\"multiple_maximal_current_records\", f\"Multiple maximal current-valid records: {ids}.\"),), dirty)\r\n   249\t        selected = maximal[0]\r\n   250\t        return ConformanceState(task_id, title, \"conformant\", head, head_tree, selected.record_id,\r\n   251\t            (_finding(\"current_record_selected\", \"Record is valid for current contract, canon, surfaces, gates, and artifacts.\", selected),), dirty)\r\n   252\t    for state_name, candidates, code, message in (\r\n   253\t        (\"needs_replan\", replan, \"contract_changed\", \"Current contract revision or semantic hash differs from prior evidence.\"),\r\n   254\t        (\"needs_human\", human, \"human_approval_missing\", \"Required human approval is missing.\"),\r\n   255\t        (\"needs_revalidation\", stale, \"evidence_stale\", \"Prior evidence exists but is not current for HEAD.\"),\r\n     1\t# CURRENT STATE — No Safe Circle AI Pipeline\n     2\t\n     3\t> Update this file whenever a milestone or important implementation slice changes.\n     4\t\n     5\tLast updated: 2026-08-23, for Stage 4C OpenAI/Codex AgentRuntime and ArchitectureReview migration on `provider-adapters`.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Current Phase\n     8\t\n     9\t**Architecture Correction Phase 3 — COMPLETE AND MERGED.**\n    10\t\n    11\tPhase 3A — Evidence-Derived Current Conformance Evaluator — is complete.\n    12\t\n    13\tPhase 3B — First Real Production Baseline — is complete.\n    14\t\n    15\tPhase 3 was fast-forward merged into `main` at:\n    16\t\n    17\t```text\n    18\t43fdf0a163e281204906abd43a241db211587a0f\n    19\t```\n    20\t\n    21\t**Provider-Neutral Execution Crew Plan — Stage 4A: MAPPING, ENFORCEMENT, AND TRANSPORT-EVALUATION DECISIONS COMPLETE.**\n    22\t\n    23\tThe current development branch is:\n    24\t\n    25\t```text\n    26\tprovider-adapters\n    27\t```\n    28\t\n    29\tThe Stage 3 foundation now implements:\n    30\t\n    31\t- provider-neutral immutable `AgentInvocationRequest` and `AgentResult` contracts;\n    32\t- semantic capability and write-boundary contracts;\n    33\t- `low_cost`, `standard`, and `high_reasoning` model capability classes;\n    34\t- strict provider configuration loading and validation;\n    35\t- bounded request budgets and normalized failure classifications;\n    36\t- strict JSON value and supported-schema validation;\n    37\t- atomic, no-overwrite immutable run artifacts;\n    38\t- provider-neutral base interfaces;\n    39\t- a deterministic, side-effect-free `FakeProvider`;\n    40\t- an adversarial regression suite covering provider trust boundaries, path safety, schema failures, immutable artifacts, malformed provider values, and historical-directory protection.\n    41\t\n    42\tThe Stage 3 implementation is integrated; Stage 4A changes are documentation and decision work only.\n    43\t\n    44\tLive CLI discovery is complete. Non-production-write structured-output success probes completed for Claude Code and OpenAI/Codex. The provider-transport adopt-versus-build spike is also complete: `agent-mux` and `agent-shell` were evaluated and are not being adopted as production dependencies. ADR-035 was amended on 2026-08-23 to keep `AgentRequest` schema 1.0 and its required integer `turn_limit`, with explicit provider-specific enforcement mappings.\n    45\t\n    46\t**Stage 4B.2 — Practical Repository Read/Search** extends the existing Claude adapter for this trusted single-user local environment. `repository_read` maps to Claude `Read`; `repository_search` maps to Claude `Glob` and `Grep`; their combination exposes all three. Repository-capable calls use the actual source repository root (`/workspace` in Docker), while empty-capability calls retain their fresh empty temporary workspace and no-tool behavior. Validated `context_paths` are accepted only with repository capability and become prompt guidance rather than a hardened sandbox boundary.\n    47\t\n    48\t**Stage 4C — OpenAI/Codex Provider and ArchitectureReview Migration** adds `OpenAICodexProvider` behind generic AgentRuntime. The active OpenAI ArchitectureReview path now constructs task-neutral `AgentInvocationRequest` values and calls `AgentRunner`; provider subprocess, JSONL/final-output parsing, usage normalization, timeout translation, and failure normalization live in AgentRuntime. Invocation audit artifacts are nested under each ArchitectureReview run. TaskExecution is not involved.\n    49\t\n    50\tAgentRuntime `approved_command_execution`, repository writing, web access, non-null token limits, provider fallback, and production orchestration remain unsupported. The Codex ArchitectureReview repository read/search implementation uses Codex's ordinary read-only shell/file inspection inside the externally read-only `codex-review` Docker environment; that is not approved command execution. Stage 4C remains the OpenAI/Codex Provider stage.\n    51\t\n    52\tArchitectureReview generated runs and provider-latest views are separated under `outputs/claude/` and `outputs/codex/`; those provider-specific latest views retain convenience copies. Global `outputs/latest/` contains only one atomic `LATEST.json` pointer identifying the most recently completed provider-scoped run across providers. Manifests record the explicit provider namespace, resume cannot cross it, and failed/partial runs do not publish latest. Each provider retains eight independent reviewer roles. New independent reviewers ignore prior review opinions even when summarized in architecture/current-state documentation, while still using implemented architecture, accepted decisions, and current documented facts as evidence to judge independently. This preserves review provenance and supports a later Claude-versus-Codex comparison without implementing that comparison pipeline.\n    53\t\n    54\t**Provider-Neutral Execution Crew Plan — Stage 4: Implement Claude Code and OpenAI/Codex adapters against the same AgentRuntime fixtures.**\n    55\t\n    56\tThe accepted Stage 4 turn-budget mapping is:\n    57\t\n    58\t- Claude: `turn_limit=N` -> native `--max-turns N`, also bounded by external `timeout_seconds`;\n    59\t- OpenAI/Codex: no observed native turn limit, so use temporary `OPENAI_SECONDS_PER_TURN = 30` and `effective_timeout_seconds = min(timeout_seconds, turn_limit * 30)`;\n    60\t- these mappings are bounded-execution controls, not cross-provider-equivalent units of model work;\n    61\t- any non-null `token_limit` remains unsupported and fails closed.\n    62\t\n    63\tNo production `ExecutionCrew` role orchestration, Unity execution by an agent, GER integration, task selection, dependency readiness, autonomous dispatch, automatic Git commit/merge behavior, or live provider fallback has been enabled.\n    64\t\n    65\tArchitecture Correction Phase 3 remains intentionally fail-closed for execution:\n    66\t\n    67\t```text\n    68\tTASK READINESS: UNAVAILABLE — DISPATCH POLICY NOT ENABLED\n    69\t```\n    70\t\n    71\tand:\n    72\t\n    73\t```text\n    74\tEXECUTION AUTHORIZATION: DENIED\n    75\t```\n    76\t\n    77\tEvidence-derived conformance has been proven for `NSC-023`, but a conformant task does not establish dependency readiness or execution authority.\n    78\t\n   629\t## Immediate Next Goal\n   630\t\n   631\t### Migrate ArchitectureReview through generic AgentRuntime using Claude\n   632\t\n   633\tStage 4B.2 repository read/search and Stage 4B.3 responsibility separation are complete. `AgentInvocationRequest` schema 1.0 is generic; `TaskExecutionRequest` schema 1.0 separately owns NSC identity; `AgentResult` remains schema 1.0. `ProviderOutputInvalid` normalization is already implemented.\n   634\t\n   635\tThe next useful production proof is to migrate ArchitectureReview through AgentRuntime using the existing Claude adapter. That later slice should retain ArchitectureReview workflow identity above AgentRuntime and should not invent a task identity. The OpenAI/Codex provider remains unimplemented.\n   636\t\n   637\tCurrent provider budget policy remains:\n   638\t\n   639\t- Claude Code: native `--max-turns N` plus external `timeout_seconds`;\n   640\t- OpenAI/Codex: `effective_timeout_seconds = min(timeout_seconds, turn_limit * 30)` using the temporary 30-seconds-per-turn-budget-unit policy;\n   641\t- non-null `token_limit`: fail closed;\n   642\t- no automatic model/provider fallback.\n   643\t\n   644\tStage 4 must remain bounded:\n   645\t\n   646\t- no provider-specific task contracts or role schemas;\n   647\t- no automatic provider fallback that changes task meaning;\n   648\t- no production `ExecutionCrew` role orchestration yet;\n   649\t- no real gameplay task execution yet;\n   650\t- no Unity validation delegated to a model;\n   651\t- no Phase 3 evidence publication by an adapter;\n   652\t- no dependency readiness;\n   653\t- no dispatch authorization;\n   654\t- no automatic merge.\n   655\t\n   656\tArchitecture Correction Phase 3 authority remains active:\n   657\t\n   658\t- `NSC-023` derives as `conformant`;\n   659\t- readiness remains unavailable;\n   660\t- authorization remains denied;\n   661\t- no worker, provider, runtime, or future adapter result establishes completion, readiness, or dispatch authority.\n   662\t\n   663\tNo real production revalidation record exists yet. Do not fabricate a gameplay, contract, GDD, scene, implementation, or test change merely to produce one. The first legitimate relevant change will exercise the production revalidation path.\n   664\t\n   665\t## Real Gameplay Task Selection After the Evidence Proof\n   666\t\n   667\tThe first gameplay implementation task is **not automatically selected** by this document, the graph, or reviewer consensus.\n   668\t\n   669\t`NSC-037` was discussed during architecture review as a possible delivery-lane experiment. It is not the committed gameplay priority.\n   670\t\n   671\t`NSC-003` remains a possible high-leverage gameplay anchor, but it should not be handed to a worker unchanged merely because its task contract currently says `single_agent`.\n   672\t\n   673\tBefore implementing NSC-003, human review should resolve:\n   674\t\n   675\t- which Input Action owns click-to-move/select;\n   676\t- arbitration among UI click, movement, Fireball, Frost Field, Force Wave, and door selection;\n   677\t- click versus held-pointer steering;\n   678\t- destination replacement and cancellation;\n   679\t- approach/arrival semantics;\n   680\t- movement pathing expectations;\n   681\t- movement-restriction ownership/release semantics.\n   682\t\n   683\tHuman review should also decide whether NSC-003 should be superseded by smaller contracts, for example:\n   684\t\n   685\t- runtime input and shared pointer-projection foundation;\n   686\t- mouse-directed movement, restriction, reset, and suspension.\n   687\t\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n     2\t\"\"\"Static checks for the authoritative DoorPrototype Unity scene location.\"\"\"\r\n     3\t\r\n     4\tfrom pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath\r\n     5\timport re\r\n     6\timport subprocess\r\n     7\timport sys\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t\r\n    10\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\r\n    11\tSCENE_PATH = \"Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\r\n    12\tMETA_PATH = SCENE_PATH + \".meta\"\r\n    13\tEXPECTED_GUID = \"92dbd0a3e6c18e245896a66c5120379d\"\r\n    14\tOBSOLETE_DIRECTORY = Path(\"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes\")\r\n    15\tBUILDER_PATH = Path(\"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\")\r\n    16\tCAMERA_FIXTURES = (\r\n    17\t    Path(\"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\"),\r\n    18\t    Path(\"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/CommittedSceneCameraConformanceTests.cs\"),\r\n    19\t)\r\n    20\t\r\n    21\t\r\n    22\tdef read(relative_path: Path | str) -> str:\r\n    23\t    path = ROOT / relative_path\r\n    24\t    if not path.is_file():\r\n    25\t        raise AssertionError(f\"Required file does not exist: {relative_path}\")\r\n    26\t    return path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\r\n    27\t\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\tdef tracked_files() -> list[str]:\r\n    30\t    result = subprocess.run(\r\n    31\t        [\"git\", \"ls-files\", \"-z\"],\r\n    32\t        cwd=ROOT,\r\n    33\t        check=True,\r\n    34\t        capture_output=True,\r\n    35\t    )\r\n    36\t    return [path.decode(\"utf-8\") for path in result.stdout.split(b\"\\0\") if path]\r\n    37\t\r\n    38\t\r\n    39\tdef main() -> int:\r\n    40\t    tracked = tracked_files()\r\n    41\t    tracked_scenes = [path for path in tracked if PurePosixPath(path).name == \"DoorPrototype.unity\"]\r\n    42\t    if tracked_scenes != [SCENE_PATH]:\r\n    43\t        raise AssertionError(\r\n    44\t            f\"Expected exactly one tracked DoorPrototype.unity at {SCENE_PATH}; found {tracked_scenes}\"\r\n    45\t        )\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\t    if not (ROOT / SCENE_PATH).is_file():\r\n    48\t        raise AssertionError(f\"Authoritative scene does not exist: {SCENE_PATH}\")\r\n    49\t\r\n    50\t    meta = read(META_PATH)\r\n    51\t    guid_match = re.search(r\"(?m)^guid:\\s*([0-9a-fA-F]+)\\s*$\", meta)\r\n    52\t    if guid_match is None or guid_match.group(1) != EXPECTED_GUID:\r\n    53\t        actual = guid_match.group(1) if guid_match else \"missing\"\r\n    54\t        raise AssertionError(f\"Expected {META_PATH} GUID {EXPECTED_GUID}; found {actual}\")\r\n    55\t\r\n    56\t    obsolete_paths = (\r\n    57\t        OBSOLETE_DIRECTORY / \"DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\n    58\t        OBSOLETE_DIRECTORY / \"DoorPrototype.unity.meta\",\r\n    59\t        Path(str(OBSOLETE_DIRECTORY) + \".meta\"),\r\n    60\t    )\r\n    61\t    for obsolete_path in obsolete_paths:\r\n    62\t        if (ROOT / obsolete_path).exists():\r\n    63\t            raise AssertionError(f\"Obsolete Unity asset path still exists: {obsolete_path}\")\r\n    64\t\r\n    65\t    builder = read(BUILDER_PATH)\r\n    66\t    if not re.search(r'private const string SceneFolder\\s*=\\s*\"Assets/Scenes\"\\s*;', builder):\r\n    67\t        raise AssertionError(\"Production scene builder does not use Assets/Scenes\")\r\n    68\t    if not re.search(r'ScenePath\\s*=\\s*SceneFolder\\s*\\+\\s*\"/DoorPrototype\\.unity\"', builder):\r\n    69\t        raise AssertionError(\"Production scene builder does not build DoorPrototype.unity in SceneFolder\")\r\n    70\t\r\n    71\t    for fixture_path in CAMERA_FIXTURES:\r\n    72\t        fixture = read(fixture_path)\r\n    73\t        if SCENE_PATH not in fixture:\r\n    74\t            raise AssertionError(f\"Camera test fixture does not use {SCENE_PATH}: {fixture_path}\")\r\n    75\t\r\n    76\t    obsolete_scene_path = (OBSOLETE_DIRECTORY / \"DoorPrototype.unity\").as_posix()\r\n    77\t    active_files = [\r\n    78\t        path for path in (ROOT / \"Assets\").rglob(\"*.cs\")\r\n    79\t        if path.is_file()\r\n    80\t    ]\r\n    81\t    offenders = [\r\n    82\t        path.relative_to(ROOT).as_posix()\r\n    83\t        for path in active_files\r\n    84\t        if obsolete_scene_path in path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\r\n    85\t    ]\r\n    86\t    if offenders:\r\n    87\t        raise AssertionError(f\"Active production/test files reference obsolete scene path: {offenders}\")\r\n    88\t\r\n    89\t    print(\"PASS: DoorPrototype scene location and Unity asset identity are authoritative.\")\r\n    90\t    return 0\r\n    66\t             EVALUATOR\r\n    67\t                ↓\r\n    68\t        repeated failures\r\n    69\t                ↓\r\n    70\t         CIRCUIT BREAKER\r\n    71\t                ↓\r\n    72\t           Human Review\r\n    73\t```\r\n    74\t\r\n    75\tThe Circuit Breaker allows a maximum of **three refinement attempts**. If the system cannot self-correct within that limit, the task is escalated for human review.\r\n    76\t\r\n    77\t## What Happened During the Run\r\n    78\t\r\n    79\t### Implementation Pass 1 — Generator\r\n    80\t\r\n    81\tThe Assignment 5 implementation agent generated the first camera implementation.\r\n    82\t\r\n    83\tIt modified:\r\n    84\t\r\n    85\t- `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs`\r\n    86\t- `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs`\r\n    87\t\r\n    88\tThe implementation changed the camera to orthographic and added tests.\r\n    89\t\r\n    90\t### Evaluation Pass 1 — Static Pass\r\n    91\t\r\n    92\tThe Evaluator found that the implementation satisfied all four static acceptance criteria:\r\n    93\t\r\n    94\t- orthographic projection,\r\n    95\t- fixed isometric presentation,\r\n    96\t- no free camera rotation,\r\n    97\t- correct scope.\r\n    98\t\r\n    99\tHowever, the checked-in Unity scene was still stale, so I rebuilt the Door Prototype scene in Unity and tested the result manually.\r\n   100\t\r\n   101\t### Unity Runtime Test 1 — Failure\r\n   102\t\r\n   103\tThe camera was orthographic, but the game was not usable:\r\n   104\t\r\n   105\t- the camera faced the wrong direction;\r\n   106\t- the camera did not follow the player;\r\n   107\t- the static evaluator had interpreted “fixed camera” too narrowly.\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\tI recorded this as:\r\n   110\t\r\n   111\t`Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback000.json`\r\n   112\t\r\n   113\tThe pipeline was updated so human Unity runtime failures could re-enter the GER loop as evaluation feedback.\r\n   114\t\r\n   115\t### Implementation Pass 2 — Refiner\r\n   116\t\r\n   117\tThe Assignment 5 implementation agent was reused as the Refiner.\r\n   118\t\r\n   119\tIt created:\r\n   120\t\r\n   121\t- `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/IsometricCameraFollow.cs`\r\n   122\t\r\n   123\tand modified the scene builder and camera tests.\r\n   124\t\r\n   125\tThe camera could now translate with the player while preserving a fixed isometric orientation.\r\n   126\t\r\n   127\t### Evaluation Pass 2 — Static Pass\r\n   128\t\r\n   129\tThe Evaluator again passed the implementation statically.\r\n   130\t\r\n   131\tI rebuilt and tested the scene in Unity again.\r\n   132\t\r\n   133\t### Unity Runtime Test 2 — Failure\r\n   134\t\r\n   135\tThe camera still did not frame the game correctly. The player-follow behavior existed, but the viewing side and framing were wrong and the starting door was no longer properly visible.\r\n   136\t\r\n   137\tI recorded this separately as:\r\n   138\t\r\n   139\t`Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback001.json`\r\n   140\t\r\n   141\tRuntime feedback files are preserved as an append-only history:\r\n   142\t\r\n   143\t```text\r\n   144\truntime_feedback000.json\r\n   145\truntime_feedback001.json\r\n   146\truntime_feedback002.json\r\n   147\t...\r\n   148\t```\r\n   149\t\r\n   150\t### Implementation Pass 3 — Refiner Made No Progress\r\n   151\t\r\n   152\tThe Refiner reported `implemented`, but it made **no observed changes under `Assets/`**.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
