s to 24 turns / Raise parallel reconciliation workers to 24 turns\n9523612 2026-08-20 Add max-turn recovery to parallel reconciliation\ne8a207f 2026-08-20 Add max-turn recovery to parallel verification\nce3d052 2026-08-20 Allow for more concurrency for the verification and reconciliation\n73540ee 2026-08-20 Add complete routing registry to parallel reconciliation\n144c1ba 2026-08-20 Clean up parallel reconciliation console output\na5e2c28 2026-08-20 Add domain-parallel verification pipeline\naffff2e 2026-08-20 Add domain-parallel reconciliation pipeline\ndfea31a 2026-08-20 Harden verification dependency and writer-lock semantics\n40040fb 2026-08-20 Harden spell reset and feedback closure\ndc4a95d 2026-08-20 Close final verification false positives\ncce5a2c 2026-08-20 Harden final graph-edge ownership\n938e6de 2026-08-20 Harden verification semantics and coverage\n7e00645 2026-08-20 Harden reconciliation canonical coverage\n069d23c 2026-08-20 Align package-lock evidence boundary\n852d08c 2026-08-20 Close verification ownership and process gaps\nd8a6a89 2026-08-20 Clarify restart, victory, and navigation ownership\n5d70093 2026-08-20 Harden reconciliation dependency preflight\nf6fe091 2026-08-19 Clarify build, navigation, feedback, and graph prerequisites\ne1bc32a 2026-08-19 Clarify shared gameplay ownership and reconciliation boundaries\nd82cca2 2026-08-19 Fix exclusive resource key validation in reconciliation verification\n3fb34ab 2026-08-19 Normalize contradictory reconciliation execution scope\nb2bfaa9 2026-08-19 Add typed non-code requirements and structural refinement\nde86121 2026-08-19 Add requirement representation taxonomy\nd17ac45 2026-08-19 Improve verification Refiner sizing and recovery\n42c799e 2026-08-19 Allow Unity package manifest as reconciliation evidence\n5bf289c 2026-08-19 Add execution-scope auditing and simplify reconciliation outputs\n1355db9 2026-08-19 Add verification recovery for refined reconciliation runs\n58a757f 2026-08-19 Add multi-model reconciliation verification crew\nf651627 2026-08-19 Make reconciliation outputs immutable and add graph-delta boundary\n6465b1b 2026-08-18 Add structural repair for dangling reconciliation dependencies\nd307b1d 2026-08-18 Harden reconciliation source boundaries\nc262902 2026-08-18 Fix reconciliation dependency validation and preserve raw output\n03749c5 2026-08-18 Add reconciliation agent for work graph bootstrap\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"alternative_architecture\":{\"description\":\"Replace the milestone-first platform with a thin feature-delivery kernel: separate stable product requirements from engineering policy and generated repository inventory; plan one human-approved vertical slice at a time; run one coding agent in an isolated branch; gate it with deterministic Git/Unity checks, one fresh semantic reviewer, and targeted human Play Mode review; record a compact delivery receipt; use requirement-level impact links for later GDD changes; add scheduling only after several successful deliveries.\",\"needed\":true,\"why_better\":\"It preserves the project’s strongest safety boundaries while eliminating global reconciliation, duplicated state, correlated verifier swarms, and provider infrastructure from the critical path to gameplay.\"},\"architecture_summary\":\"Inspection is complete. The current design has sound safety primitives but is not fundamentally sound as an autonomous Unity delivery architecture in its present organization. Its canon/state model conflates product design, engineering process, and dated repository facts; its verification independence is heavily prompt-anchored and same-family; and the implemented pipeline cannot write, run Unity, dispatch, or merge a gameplay task. The final verdict will recommend a materially thinner feature-delivery architecture and a mouse-movement vertical slice.\",\"biggest_uncertainty\":\"Actual model-token invoices are not stored in a normalized comparable form, so cost severity is inferred from the number, turn limits, prompt sizes, and retry topology of model invocations rather than measured spend.\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"do_not_build_yet\":[\"Continuous supervisor\",\"Parallel workers/worktree pool\",\"GitHub project synchronization\",\"Progressive Decomposer/Artifact Authority platform\",\"More provider migrations or provider-comparison review infrastructure\",\"Another global reconciliation run\"],\"evidence\":[{\"observation\":\"All inspected deterministic commands left HEAD/tree clean; taskcontrol validates 37 structurally valid contracts, but readiness remains unavailable and dispatch authority disabled.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py\"},{\"observation\":\"Sixteen task contracts plus RESOURCE_GROUPS, PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS, and GDD canon reference a scene path deleted by commit 484e66a; structural validation still passes.\",\"path\":\"Tasks/; Pipeline/TaskGraph/RESOURCE_GROUPS.yaml; Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\"},{\"observation\":\"Conformance compares every task record to a whole-GDD hash, so any GDD edit stales all evidenced tasks regardless of relevance.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py:164\"},{\"observation\":\"The Reconciliation prompt suite is 4,251 lines and includes dated closure instructions prescribing prior repaired conclusions.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/Reconciliation/prompts/\"},{\"observation\":\"Parallel reconciliation supplies prior routing keys and the same complete key registry to all nine workers; verifier diversity defaults only to Claude opus/sonnet aliases.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/Reconciliation/parallel_reconciliation_agent.py:617; Pipeline/Reconciliation/verification_crew.py:71\"},{\"observation\":\"Pipeline Python totals about 24,623 lines versus about 1,508 lines of Unity C#; history shows 56 reconciliation commits, 41 TaskGraph commits, and 21 runtime/review commits versus 7 commits touching Assets.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/; Assets/; git history\"},{\"observation\":\"Assignment 6 records two static evaluator passes followed by human Unity failures and a no-op refinement.\",\"path\":\"Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md:90\"},{\"observation\":\"CURRENT_STATE says Codex ArchitectureReview migration is implemented near the top but later says Claude migration is next and Codex is unimplemented.\",\"path\":\"Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md:48; Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md:631\"}],\"gdd_iteration_concerns\":[\"The GDD contains gameplay intent, agent workflow policy, package choices, build configuration, and dated repository inventory in one root-canon file. Routine engineering changes therefore masquerade as game-design changes.\",\"Whole-document canon hashing creates global invalidation instead of requirement-scoped impact.\",\"Sequential RAG chunk IDs are deterministic but not durable requirement identities across heading insertion/reordering.\",\"Tasks copy GDD prose and bootstrap repository observations, so they become independent stale replicas.\",\"There is no demonstrated workflow that maps a changed GDD clause to only affected contracts, implementation surfaces, tests, and evidence.\",\"The scene relocation proves synchronization is not transactional: code/tests and evidence moved while canon, task locks, and project requirements did not.\"],\"human_intervention_points\":[\"Approve ambiguous mechanics and input arbitration before implementation; NSC-003 currently needs these decisions.\",\"Own architecture and canon changes where product intent is affected.\",\"Run Play Mode/visual/input-feel/readability/balance checks that automation cannot establish.\",\"Inspect scene/prefab/package/build-setting changes and resolve Unity serialization conflicts.\",\"Review and merge initially; merge automation should wait until repeated end-to-end success.\",\"Triage circuit-breaker escalations and decide whether failures mean repair, contract change, or design change.\"],\"hypothetical_failure_solutions\":[\"Exact-type, polymorphic-container, Windows device-name, and deep JSON hardening in AgentRuntime protects adversarial provider-boundary cases not observed in game delivery.\",\"Incomparable evidence-record ancestry, cycle, and ambiguity handling is exercised synthetically but not by a real production revalidation history.\",\"GitHub mirroring, leases, multi-worktree scheduling, merge queues, and parallel conflict claims address future scale; none is needed for the current single-worker game.\",\"Artifact Authority and style GER protect future AI-authored design/content, but the current graph has zero artifact tasks.\",\"Eight-role ArchitectureReview provider provenance and potential cross-provider comparison do not advance gameplay delivery.\"],\"missing_components\":[\"A real end-to-end gameplay delivery lane from approved contract through write-capable implementation, Unity validation, review, merge, and evidence.\",\"Stable requirement/clause identities and scoped change-impact links.\",\"A write-capable, externally contained worker path and allowlisted deterministic command execution.\",\"Production ExecutionCrew/GER integration or a much thinner equivalent.\",\"Attempt/lease state and restartable recovery for one real task.\",\"A deterministic referential check spanning canon-described repository paths, task resource claims, builder targets, and actual assets.\",\"Measured per-feature token, latency, retry, and human-minute telemetry.\",\"Production evidence creation automation; only NSC-023 has a committed baseline and no real revalidation exists.\"],\"next_slice\":{\"deliverables\":[\"Human-approved one-page input decision covering click/hold semantics, UI/gameplay arbitration, destination replacement/cancellation, arrival tolerance, and pathing assumptions.\",\"Supersede/split NSC-003 so the first contract covers shared pointer projection plus visible click-to-destination/hold-steer movement; leave restriction/reset/suspend interfaces in a follow-up contract unless required by the implementation seam.\",\"Correct the authoritative scene path across GDD engineering facts, task/resource claims, and project requirements, with one deterministic cross-representation referential check.\",\"Implement the slice in one isolated branch using Input Actions, the shared gameplay-plane projection, scene-builder wiring, and the committed Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity artifact.\",\"Run clean targeted Edit/Play Mode validation, preserve XML outside the worktree during execution, obtain human movement-feel approval, perform one fresh diff review, merge, and publish one compact delivery receipt.\"],\"proof_of_value\":\"Within one working day, an approved brief becomes merged, visibly playable mouse-directed movement with clean Unity evidence, bounded model usage, no global reconciliation, and no manual repair of duplicated state. Record elapsed time, model invocations/tokens where available, repair count, and human minutes.\",\"title\":\"NSC-003A mouse movement vertical slice through a thin delivery lane\",\"why\":\"It is player-visible, unlocks Fireball/Frost Field/door targeting, directly tests the highest-value agent workflow, and exposes Unity/input/state-change problems earlier than another infrastructure slice.\"},\"observed_failure_solutions\":[\"Runtime evidence re-entering GER addresses the camera’s two actual static-pass/runtime-fail incidents.\",\"No-op detection and circuit breakers address the observed refiner claim that made no Assets change, although delta must remain tied to a specific unresolved failure to avoid churn.\",\"The non-saving in-memory scene-builder seam and clean Unity runner address observed canonical-scene mutation risk from builder tests.\",\"Production GDDRAG freshness/integrity replaces the actually stale July Assignment 4 knowledge base.\",\"Scene centralization plus asset/meta identity checks addresses the earlier duplicate authoritative-scene ambiguity.\",\"Raw-output preservation, bounded retries, finding identity, and deterministic graph/schema checks address numerous observed reconciliation parse, max-turn, dangling-edge, attribution, and refinement failures.\",\"Removing mutable task status from contracts prevents the discovered one-line authorization vulnerability, though no bad autonomous dispatch actually occurred.\"],\"overall_verdict\":\"partially_unsound\",\"overengineering\":[\"Roughly 24.6k lines of production pipeline Python precede a single write-capable gameplay execution lane.\",\"Global reconciliation can use nine generation workers plus fifteen parallel auditors, refiners, selective pass 2, and recovery, for a 37-task graph.\",\"The 4,251-line reconciliation prompt suite encodes accumulated closure patches, increasing maintenance and anchoring.\",\"AgentRuntime spends substantial complexity on hostile polymorphic JSON/path cases in a trusted single-user environment while repository writing and approved command execution remain unsupported.\",\"ArchitectureReview provider migration proves transport reuse, not game-development throughput.\",\"WORK_ID_MAP and persisted resource-group membership duplicate mappings derivable from task contracts; multiple current-state documents also duplicate operational status.\"],\"state_and_authority_concerns\":[\"Necessary boundaries are: human-approved product canon; a bounded task/feature contract; integrated Git tree; isolated attempt state; deterministic test/runtime evidence; human experiential approval; derived readiness/merge state.\",\"Task definitions must not own completion truth, and model/provider claims must not own test or merge truth; these are strong current boundaries.\",\"GDD root canon should not own dated repository inventory or detailed pipeline architecture. Those belong in generated repository facts and engineering policy respectively.\",\"Reconciliation snapshots are useful audit history, but Tasks, WORK_ID_MAP, RESOURCE_GROUPS, PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS, GDD copies, CURRENT_STATE, milestone docs, and current reconciliation views duplicate facts and drift.\",\"Manually selected conformance surfaces can omit a causal dependency; whole-GDD hashing simultaneously invalidates too broadly. The model is both under- and over-sensitive.\",\"GitHub operational state would be acceptable as a dashboard, but mirroring it into another local operational state should be avoided until one owner is explicit.\",\"Human approval is currently broad enough that architecture, every merge, scene inspection, playtesting, balance, and integration remain human responsibilities; this is assisted development, not high autonomy.\"],\"strong_decisions\":[\"Deterministic tools own graph math, Git identity, schema checks, test execution facts, and clean-tree checks.\",\"Workers and providers cannot self-declare delivery, conformance, readiness, or authorization.\",\"Runtime/Unity evidence can override a semantic/static pass.\",\"Task definitions are separated from completion evidence.\",\"Branches/worktrees before parallelism and conservative Unity asset locking are appropriate.\",\"RAG is current-canon retrieval, not repository-state truth.\",\"Progressive decomposition and explicit human authority for missing design are sensible in principle.\",\"Starting with one worker and bounding retries is correct.\"],\"structural_flaws\":[\"The architecture treats evolving design mainly as snapshot reconciliation and global invalidation, not routine scoped change management.\",\"Verification independence is overstated: workers share canon, candidate framing, prior routing keys, full key registry, the same provider family, and increasingly prescriptive closure prompts.\",\"Unioning all verifier findings lowers false-negative risk but magnifies false-positive cost; repeated prompt patches show unstable convergence.\",\"The production critical path is absent: no write-capable task execution, Unity invocation by orchestration, production GER, readiness, dispatch, or merge.\",\"Deterministic checks are strong at artifact shape and transport boundaries but weak at cross-representation semantic referential integrity, demonstrated by the deleted scene path.\",\"No-op-means-failure is too coarse: Assignment 6’s final pass added a null-target warning/test while the actual runtime issue had already been repaired elsewhere, showing pressure toward unrelated churn.\",\"The milestone order optimized architecture assurance before feature throughput and has become self-reinforcing.\"],\"throughput_assessment\":\"Current near-term leverage is low. The repository can retrieve canon, validate graph shape, harden model transport, and prove one camera baseline, but it cannot autonomously advance any gameplay task. Dispatch is disabled, workers cannot write or run approved commands, Unity/GER is not integrated, and only one task has production evidence. The existing machinery may improve assurance once attached to a delivery lane, but it is not presently credible for turning weeks into days. A thin single-feature lane could plausibly create material leverage quickly; the planned supervisor/decomposer/GitHub/parallel milestones would not.\",\"verdict_reason\":\"The core philosophy is sound, but the implemented architecture is partially unsound because its moving-canon/state synchronization model has already drifted, its semantic verification is correlated and prompt-anchored, and most investment sits outside the gameplay-delivery critical path. Keep the deterministic evidence and human-authority ideas; reorganize around one real feature at a time and delete or freeze infrastructure that does not reduce delivery time or defect escape.\"}"}}
{"type":"item.updated","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"todo_list","items":[{"text":"Verify frozen commit and map primary architecture documents","completed":true},{"text":"Inspect implementation, tests, Unity evidence, reconciliation, and relevant history","completed":true},{"text":"Assess observed versus hypothetical failures, state authority, GDD evolution, and throughput","completed":true},{"text":"Select verdict and single highest-value next slice","completed":true}]}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"alternative_architecture\":{\"description\":\"Use a thin feature-delivery kernel. State: separate stable product requirements from engineering policy and generated repository inventory; bind feature contracts only to relevant requirement IDs. Planning: select and clarify one near-term vertical slice, with scoped impact analysis for later canon changes instead of global reconciliation. Execution: one write-capable agent in an isolated branch/worktree, using externally enforced file and command permissions. Validation: Git/scope checks, clean Unity Edit/Play Mode tests, one fresh semantic diff review, then targeted human experiential review. Recovery: preserve the branch and attempt journal, feed specific failure evidence into at most two repairs, then escalate. Unity integration: explicitly distinguish in-memory builders from committed scenes/prefabs and require non-mutating validation. Add deterministic scheduling only after several successful deliveries.\",\"needed\":true,\"why_better\":\"It preserves the strongest current safety boundaries while removing global verifier swarms, duplicated state, prompt anchoring, and provider infrastructure from the gameplay critical path.\"},\"architecture_summary\":\"The architecture contains sound safety primitives but is not sound enough, as currently organized and implemented, for autonomous Unity delivery. It is assurance-heavy and delivery-light: canon retrieval, graph validation, evidence modeling, reconciliation, and provider transport exist, but no production path can write a gameplay change, invoke Unity, perform GER, derive readiness, dispatch, or merge. Its moving-canon model is especially weak because product design, engineering policy, and dated repository facts are mixed together and synchronized through duplicated artifacts.\",\"biggest_uncertainty\":\"Actual model spend is not normalized or retained comparably. Cost severity is inferred from prompt sizes, worker counts, turn limits, retries, and history rather than invoices. Feature throughput has also never been measured through a complete production delivery.\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"do_not_build_yet\":[\"Continuous supervisor or autonomous scheduler\",\"Parallel workers and worktree pools\",\"GitHub Issues/Projects synchronization\",\"Progressive Decomposer and Artifact Authority platform\",\"More provider migrations or cross-provider comparison infrastructure\",\"Another full-project reconciliation run\"],\"evidence\":[{\"observation\":\"At the frozen clean HEAD, taskcontrol validates 37 contracts, but readiness is explicitly unavailable and zero tasks are authorized for dispatch.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py\"},{\"observation\":\"The authoritative scene moved to Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity in commit 484e66a, but 16 task contracts, RESOURCE_GROUPS, PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS, and GDD canon still reference the deleted nested scene. Structural task validation nevertheless passes.\",\"path\":\"Tasks/; Pipeline/TaskGraph/RESOURCE_GROUPS.yaml; Pipeline/TaskGraph/PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.yaml; Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\"},{\"observation\":\"Current conformance hashes the entire GDD and marks evidence stale when that hash changes, regardless of whether the edit affects the task.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py:164\"},{\"observation\":\"The production reconciliation prompt suite totals 4,251 lines and contains dated closure sections prescribing conclusions repaired during earlier rounds.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/Reconciliation/prompts/\"},{\"observation\":\"Nine reconciliation workers receive prior routing hints and the same complete key registry. Verifier diversity defaults to Claude opus and sonnet aliases, preserving provider-family and prompt correlation.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/Reconciliation/parallel_reconciliation_agent.py:617; Pipeline/Reconciliation/verification_crew.py:71\"},{\"observation\":\"Parallel verification defines nine domain coverage audits plus six evidence/structure/execution audits before refiners and selective re-verification.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/Reconciliation/parallel_verification_crew.py:196\"},{\"observation\":\"Production pipeline Python totals approximately 24,623 lines, compared with approximately 1,508 lines of Unity C# game code.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/; Assets/\"},{\"observation\":\"History contains 56 commits touching Reconciliation, 41 touching TaskGraph, and 21 touching AgentRuntime/TaskExecution/ArchitectureReview, versus 7 commits touching Assets.\",\"path\":\"Git history through 9f2485dca1b61360e6d02810adc71e021346496e\"},{\"observation\":\"Assignment 6 records two static evaluator passes followed by two human Unity runtime failures, then a refiner claim that made no Assets changes.\",\"path\":\"Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md:90\"},{\"observation\":\"CURRENT_STATE first says the Codex ArchitectureReview migration is implemented, then later says Claude migration is next and Codex remains unimplemented.\",\"path\":\"Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md:48; Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md:631\"},{\"observation\":\"Read-only checks executed successfully: taskcontrol validate, taskcontrol ready, NSC-023 state, and GDDRAG validate. HEAD/tree and the worktree remained unchanged; NSC-023 is the sole demonstrated conformant production task.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/NSC-023/\"}],\"gdd_iteration_concerns\":[\"The root GDD mixes gameplay intent, agent workflow policy, package choices, build configuration, and dated repository inventory. An engineering change can therefore appear to be a game-design change.\",\"Whole-document hashing creates global revalidation pressure from unrelated canon edits.\",\"Sequential RAG chunk IDs are reproducible but are not durable requirement identities across heading insertion or reordering.\",\"Task contracts copy GDD prose and bootstrap repository observations, creating stale replicas instead of durable references.\",\"No demonstrated workflow maps a changed clause to only the affected contracts, code/assets, tests, and evidence.\",\"The scene relocation proves synchronization is not transactional: production code, tests, and evidence moved while canon, resource claims, and task evidence did not.\",\"Routine GDD evolution needs a reviewed requirement-level impact workflow. Full reconciliation should be an exceptional audit, not the normal synchronization mechanism.\"],\"human_intervention_points\":[\"Approve ambiguous gameplay mechanics and input arbitration. NSC-003 currently lacks enough decisions for a safe handoff.\",\"Approve genuine canon or architecture changes rather than letting an agent infer design.\",\"Perform Play Mode, input-feel, framing, readability, animation, visual-quality, and balance judgments.\",\"Inspect scene, prefab, package, and build-setting changes where serialization or editor behavior matters.\",\"Review and merge initially; merge automation should wait for repeated delivery evidence.\",\"Decide whether a circuit-breaker failure requires repair, task rescoping, contract change, or design change.\"],\"hypothetical_failure_solutions\":[\"AgentRuntime exact-type, polymorphic-container, Windows device-name, deep-JSON, and immutable-publication hardening protects mostly adversarial transport cases not experienced during game delivery.\",\"Evidence-record cycle, incomparable-ancestry, and ambiguity logic is covered synthetically but has no real production revalidation history.\",\"GitHub mirroring, leases, merge queues, and parallel resource scheduling address future scale, not the current single-worker bottleneck.\",\"Artifact Authority and style GER address future generated design/content; the current graph has zero artifact tasks.\",\"Eight-role ArchitectureReview provider provenance and future cross-provider comparison do not advance gameplay delivery.\",\"Automatic backlog replenishment and continuous supervision protect a future autonomous queue that does not yet exist.\"],\"missing_components\":[\"A production end-to-end gameplay lane from approved contract through implementation, Unity validation, review, merge, and evidence.\",\"Stable requirement/clause identities and scoped GDD-change impact links.\",\"A write-capable worker boundary and externally enforced approved command execution.\",\"Production ExecutionCrew/GER integration, or a substantially thinner equivalent.\",\"Restartable attempt/lease state for one real task.\",\"Cross-representation referential validation covering canon-described paths, task resource claims, builders, tests, and actual Unity assets.\",\"Automated compact delivery/revalidation receipt creation.\",\"Per-feature token, latency, retry, defect, and human-minute telemetry.\",\"A real production revalidation example; only NSC-023 has a baseline.\"],\"next_slice\":{\"deliverables\":[\"Obtain a one-page human-approved input decision covering click/hold semantics, UI/gameplay arbitration, destination replacement and cancellation, arrival tolerance, and pathing expectations.\",\"Supersede or split NSC-003. Make the first contract cover shared pointer projection plus visible click-to-destination/hold-steer movement; defer restriction/reset/suspend APIs unless required by the implementation seam.\",\"Correct the authoritative scene path across GDD engineering facts, task/resource claims, and project requirements, then add one deterministic cross-representation path check.\",\"Implement the movement slice in one isolated branch using Input Actions, shared gameplay-plane projection, scene-builder wiring, and the committed Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity artifact.\",\"Run clean targeted Edit/Play Mode validation, obtain human movement-feel approval, perform one fresh semantic diff review, merge, and publish one compact delivery receipt.\"],\"proof_of_value\":\"Within one working day, an approved brief becomes merged, visibly playable mouse-directed movement with clean Unity evidence, bounded model usage, no global reconciliation, and no manual repair of duplicated operational state. Record elapsed time, model calls/tokens where available, repair count, escaped defects, and human minutes.\",\"title\":\"NSC-003A mouse movement vertical slice through a thin delivery lane\",\"why\":\"It is player-visible, unlocks Fireball, Frost Field, and door targeting, and tests the actual value proposition more directly than another infrastructure milestone.\"},\"observed_failure_solutions\":[\"Runtime evidence re-entering GER directly addresses the camera’s two static-pass/runtime-fail incidents.\",\"No-op detection and circuit breakers address the observed refiner claim that made no Assets change. Progress should, however, be tied to resolving a named failure rather than merely producing any diff.\",\"The non-saving in-memory scene-builder seam and clean Unity runner address observed canonical-scene mutation risk from builder tests.\",\"Production GDDRAG freshness and integrity replace the actually stale July Assignment 4 knowledge base.\",\"Scene centralization and meta-identity checks address the earlier duplicate authoritative-scene ambiguity.\",\"Raw-output preservation, bounded retries, finding identities, and deterministic validators address observed reconciliation parsing, max-turn, dangling-edge, attribution, and refinement failures.\",\"Separating task contracts from mutable completion status closes a discovered authority vulnerability, although no bad autonomous dispatch actually occurred.\"],\"overall_verdict\":\"partially_unsound\",\"overengineering\":[\"Approximately 24.6k lines of pipeline Python precede a single write-capable gameplay execution lane.\",\"A 37-task graph was produced through nine generation workers and up to fifteen parallel auditors, with refiners and selective pass two layered afterward.\",\"The 4,251-line reconciliation prompt suite accumulates specific closure patches, raising maintenance cost and anchoring future reviewers.\",\"AgentRuntime heavily hardens hostile JSON and path cases in a trusted single-user environment while repository writing and approved command execution remain unsupported.\",\"ArchitectureReview provider migration proves transport reuse, not game-development throughput.\",\"WORK_ID_MAP and persisted resource-group membership duplicate relationships derivable from task contracts.\",\"CURRENT_STATE, START_HERE, master context, milestone documents, ADR summaries, and reconciliation current views duplicate present-tense state and have already diverged.\"],\"state_and_authority_concerns\":[\"Necessary authorities are: human-approved product canon; bounded feature/task contracts; integrated Git state; isolated attempt state; deterministic test/runtime evidence; human experiential approval; and derived readiness/merge state.\",\"The current separation of task definition from completion evidence is sound. Model/provider claims also correctly lack test, merge, or conformance authority.\",\"Dated repository inventory and pipeline architecture should not live in root game-design canon. Put them in generated repository facts and engineering policy.\",\"Reconciliation snapshots are useful audit history, but Tasks, WORK_ID_MAP, RESOURCE_GROUPS, PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS, copied GDD prose, current-state documents, and mutable reconciliation views duplicate responsibility.\",\"Conformance is simultaneously under-sensitive and over-sensitive: manually chosen surfaces may omit causal dependencies, while a whole-GDD hash invalidates unrelated tasks.\",\"Resource-group files duplicate task claims and validate internal agreement rather than whether the referenced Unity resource still exists.\",\"GitHub may become a dashboard, but it must not become a second operational authority without a single explicit owner.\",\"The GDD assigns humans architecture, merging, scene inspection, playtesting, balance, and final integration. The resulting system is assisted development, not high autonomy, until some of those steps are safely narrowed or automated.\"],\"strong_decisions\":[\"Deterministic tools own graph computation, Git identity, schema checks, test execution facts, and clean-tree checks.\",\"Workers and providers cannot self-declare delivery, conformance, readiness, or authorization.\",\"Runtime and Unity evidence can override a semantic/static pass.\",\"Task definitions are separated from current completion truth.\",\"Branches/worktrees should precede parallelism, and Unity shared-asset locking should be conservative.\",\"RAG is correctly treated as canon retrieval rather than repository truth.\",\"Progressive decomposition and explicit human authority for missing design are sensible principles.\",\"Starting with one worker and bounding retries is appropriate.\",\"The testing policy correctly distinguishes builder capability from committed-artifact conformance.\"],\"structural_flaws\":[\"Evolving design is framed mainly as snapshot reconciliation and invalidation instead of routine scoped change management.\",\"Verification independence is overstated because workers share canon, candidate framing, prior routing keys, the key registry, provider family, and prescriptive closure prompts.\",\"Unioning every verifier finding reduces false-negative risk but amplifies false-positive cost and destabilizes reconciliation.\",\"The production critical path is missing: no write-capable task execution, orchestrated Unity run, production GER, readiness, dispatch, or merge.\",\"Deterministic checks are strongest at artifact shape and transport boundaries but miss cross-representation referential integrity, as the deleted scene path demonstrates.\",\"The no-op rule can incentivize irrelevant churn. Assignment 6’s final pass added null-target hardening while the substantive framing repair had already occurred elsewhere.\",\"The milestone sequence optimized architecture assurance before feature throughput and has become self-reinforcing.\",\"Provider-neutrality is implemented below an absent product workflow; abstraction arrived before the first production consumer that matters.\"],\"throughput_assessment\":\"Current near-term leverage is low. The system can retrieve canon, validate graph shape, inspect one camera baseline, and harden model transport, but it cannot autonomously advance gameplay. Dispatch is disabled, workers cannot write or run approved commands, Unity/GER is not integrated, and only one task has production evidence. The machinery may improve assurance after attachment to a delivery lane, but it is not currently credible for turning weeks into days. A thin single-feature lane could plausibly create major leverage quickly; the planned supervisor, decomposer, GitHub, and parallel-worker milestones would not.\",\"verdict_reason\":\"The core philosophy is sound, but the current architecture is partially unsound because its moving-canon and state-synchronization model has already drifted, semantic verification is correlated and prompt-anchored, and most investment lies outside the gameplay-delivery critical path. Preserve deterministic evidence, runtime validation, isolation, bounded retries, and human design authority. Reorganize around one real feature at a time and freeze or remove infrastructure that does not measurably reduce delivery time or escaped defects.\"}"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"todo_list","items":[{"text":"Verify frozen commit and map primary architecture documents","completed":true},{"text":"Inspect implementation, tests, Unity evidence, reconciliation, and relevant history","completed":true},{"text":"Assess observed versus hypothetical failures, state authority, GDD evolution, and throughput","completed":true},{"text":"Select verdict and single highest-value next slice","completed":true}]}}
